<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kołbacz Abbey</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1173">1173</a>–<a href="/years/1535">1535</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Kolbatz Abbey</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kołbacz Abbey was a Cistercian monastery near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/szczecin">Szczecin</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pomerania">Pomerania</a>, founded in 1173 by monks from Esrum in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a> at the invitation of the Pomeranian noble Wartislaw Świętoborzyc. It became one of the richest monasteries of the duchy and organised German settlement and farming on its lands. It was dissolved during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestant-reformation">Reformation</a> in 1535, and parts of its church survive.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kolbacz-abbey.jpg" alt="Kołbacz Abbey" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: StasiÓ Stachów · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ko%C5%82bacz,_Poland_-_panoramio_(1).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
